<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of New York added temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system on Thursday through four-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>At 1030 EST/1530 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate was quoted at 5-3/8 percent, below the central bank's new 5.50 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
